//  libs/aocnet/tests/test_repl_hunting.cpp
//
//  Gathering stage 3, part "Hunting": what the retail server sends around the hunt of a creature (tests/capture_hunting.h, generated by tools/capture/gen_hunting.py) against the typed
//  codecs of protocol/repl.
//
//    * the eighth block of a living huntable (a dynamic UInteractableComponent of three properties) of a Raven (capture 914), a Spider (758) and a Tidesnapper (1458): each reads to its
//      last bit, holds the kind's two ids and four interaction states of 1, and is written back to the exact bits.  The Raven's block with the Spider's two ids put in IS the Spider's
//      block, to the bit, and the same for the Tidesnapper: that is all worldd needs to make the block of a kind no capture opened
//    * capture 1457's corpse channel: the start (the status 0x08000001, the harvester's pawn, who channels), 204 heartbeats whose counter (the status word's top five bits) goes up by 2
//      every ~67 ms (the resource node's goes up by 3 every 100 ms), the first taking InteractingPlayer off, and the done update (the status 0xD0000004, the pawn again, nobody channeling,
//      CanInputActivate [false], all four interaction states 0) with the corpse's CombatInfo (bIsDead) and the Health stat 0
//    * the facts of the five hunts: 204 to 213 heartbeats in 13.8 to 14.8 s, the counter of the done update one or two steps of 33 ms after the last heartbeat's (one when the done
//      update comes less than ~50 ms after it, two when it comes later), one storage event and one durability update in each result frame
// ============================================================================
